<Layout title="Download Ticker for Mac | Apple Silicon DMG" description="Download Ticker 1.0 directly as a DMG for Apple Silicon Macs running macOS 26+. Installation steps, signing status and SHA-256 checksum."><article class="wrap page"><p class="eyebrow">Download for Mac</p><h1>Put Ticker<br/>in your menu bar.</h1><p class="lede">Free download for Apple Silicon (M1 and later), running macOS 26 or newer.</p><a href="/downloads/Ticker-1.0-arm64.dmg" download class={buttonVariants({className:"large-button"})}>Download Ticker.dmg</a><p class="fine">Ticker 1.0 · 372 KB · Apple Silicon only</p><div class="prose"><h2>Install in three steps</h2><ol><li>Open the downloaded DMG.</li><li>Drag Ticker to the Applications shortcut.</li><li>Open Ticker from Applications. Its selected token appears in the menu bar.</li></ol><h2 id="security">Developer signing and notarization</h2><p>This release is signed with the Developer ID of Yash Garg and notarized by Apple. The DMG includes Apple’s notarization ticket so macOS can verify it during installation.</p><p>On first launch, macOS may ask you to confirm opening an app downloaded from the internet. Check that the developer is Yash Garg before opening it. If macOS reports that the app is damaged or cannot verify it, download a fresh copy and check the checksum below.</p><h2>Verify your download</h2><p>The SHA-256 checksum for this DMG is:</p><pre>e0049e30270d9ceb743c96b836b2b793b2d0990615a58fd90cf0b80a454cab23</pre><p>You can compare it in Terminal:</p><pre>shasum -a 256 ~/Downloads/Ticker-1.0-arm64.dmg</pre><p>A matching checksum confirms the file matches this release. It does not replace Apple's developer signing or notarization.</p><h2>After opening</h2><p>The default watchlist includes Bitcoin, Ethereum and Solana. Click a star to choose the menu bar token. Use + or ⌘N to search and add another token. Prices are in USD and refresh every minute when CoinGecko is available.</p><p>Read the <a href="/guides/bitcoin-price-mac-menu-bar/">setup guide</a> for the controls, or the <a href="/guides/crypto-price-refresh-stale-data/">price-data guide</a> if a quote is marked stale.</p></div></article></Layout>
